          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em conformal bootstrap program
            (
            %a{:href => "#BelavinPolyakovZamolodchikov84"}> Belavin-Polyakov-Zamolodchikov 84
            ) is an attempt to construct and classify
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theories"} conformal field theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbatively
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatizing
            the properties of their
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+product+expansion"} operator product expansion
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlation+functions"} correlation functions
          %p
            The conformal bootstrap was proposed in the 1970s as a strategy for calculating the properties of second-order
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+transitions"} phase transitions
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PolandSimmonsDuffin16"} Poland-Simmons-Duffin 16
          %p
            The generalization of the conformal bootstrap to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+field+theories"} superconformal field theories
            has the potential to provide, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large-N+limit"} large-N
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
